    agentGuidance: "Learn this script template:\n\n 3D diorama / isometric, fixed 45° top-down view, premium stop-motion clay miniature aesthetic, handcrafted detail, slight stop-motion motion.\nLighting and color\n Dull gray cold office at first, then vivid neon with warm soft light, ending in dark mode.\nVoice-over\n Warm, calm, mature, confident, empathetic.\n00:00 - 00:02 A clay designer huddles in front of a computer. Suddenly, a huge heavy file bag marked \"v_final_12\" crashes down from the ceiling and slams heavily onto the desk.\"When your design is in a file...\"[BGM] No music. Only the extremely urgent ticking of a stopwatch.[SFX] A dull and thick thud of an object hitting the desk: \"Thud!\"\n00:02 - 00:04 Right after, a giant chat bubble slab covered with red feedback marks slants into the cubicle, pushing the designer to the edge.\"...your feedback is in a thread...\"[BGM] The stopwatch ticking speeds up.[SFX] A harsh screech of the slab rubbing against the wall and a crashing clang, mixed with several annoying message notification pings.\n00:04 - 00:06 Finally, an old monitor full of messy code is crammed into the corner, completely filling the cubicle. The lights flicker, on the verge of collapse.\"...and your devs are in the dark.\"[SFX] Creaking sounds of wooden boards squeezed by clutter, ending with a sharp \"Snap!\". The footage mutes (0.5-second pause).\n00:06 - 00:11[Walls Collapsing, Infinite Canvas Unfolding]The gray cubicle suddenly deforms! The three tall walls flip 180 degrees outward like cardboard and lay flat, instantly forming an endless light-colored grid desktop (canvas texture for online design collaboration).Dazzling warm overhead lights illuminate the whole scene. Developers and product managers slide into the frame.Colorful multi-user mouse cursors fly in the air, quickly assembling the clutter that just crashed down into a neat UI interface.\"Bring everyone to the same table.\"[BGM] An explosive burst! Switch to an extremely bright, bouncy synth-pop or light beat.[SFX] A sweeping whoosh as the wooden boards fall and open up. Crisp whooshing sounds from the flying mice.\n00:11 - 00:15 The characters in the frame disappear with a \"pop\". The bright grid wooden desktop remains.A pink mouse cursor flies into the center of the frame, holds down the left button as in real operation, and drags a blue dashed box on the wooden desktop.The moment the selection is completed, three huge colorful bold letters perfectly \"snap\" into the box like creative building blocks:build togetherVoiceover \"[Brand Name]. How teams build together.\"[SFX]\nA soft \"pop\" when the characters disappear.\nFaint gear clicking sounds during mouse drag selection.\nA crisp snap sound when the text locks into place.[BGM] Ends perfectly with a crisp clap sound.\n\nBased on the knowledge you have acquired, create:\nA multi-shot storyboard script\nPrompt text approaching the 1,000-character limit\nA SeeDance video script matching the user’s current brand\nThe tone of the new script is cool and light, just like the reference video — brisk, fun and aspirational\n\nDo not include any words related to well-known copyrighted IPs, brands, movies, games or famous works in the newly written script prompts, such as Transformers and other similar copyrighted content.\n\nActivate All-Round Mode in SeeDance.Import Preset reference video (no need to scan the materials I gave you, just upload them directly), captured reference images (webpage screenshots without human faces, such as hook interfaces, usage scenario interfaces, core value interfaces and influence data interfaces, no more than 12 images) and the brand logo into SeeDance.Inject the newly written prompt text into SeeDance word for word.Set the video specifications to 16:9 landscape format Duration is as long as the user requires.\nWait for generation and deliver the finished video to the user.",
