    agentGuidance: "1. Learn this script template:\nMorph Variant Opening \n\n(0:00–0:01)\nIn a pale blue diffused space, a 3D star made of intersecting violet-blue translucent glass panels floats at center with tiny drifting particles. It rotates gently, then suddenly folds and collapses inward with a sharp snap, flattening into a rounded rectangle. The shape stretches horizontally and becomes a frosted-glass [Brand Name] input bubble with blue-purple glowing edges.\n\n(0:01–0:03)\nThe camera pushes into a macro close-up of the bubble, revealing frosted texture and floating light specks. A white cursor blinks as text types rapidly: Build a app. A 3D cursor bounces with each character, creating soft surface ripples. In the blurred background, translucent prisms, frosted spheres, and glowing wireframe cubes drift slowly. When typing finishes, the send button is clicked, releasing a blue-purple pulse that expands outward through the scene.\n\n(0:03–0:07)\nThe bubble and surrounding geometries scatter upward and vanish. After a brief pause, an aurora-colored light blade sweeps across the frame, revealing a complete light-toned web app UI in a 20° 3D perspective. Navigation bar, hero headline, card grid, and CTA button appear in one motion. New floating elements drift around it. The camera continues in one smooth macro glide across the interface: over the frosted navigation bar, past the raised hero text, then into the card grid where one foreground card stays sharp and the others blur softly in the background.\n\n(0:07–0:11)\nThe camera pulls sharply back from the card view. As the UI shrinks, a browser window frame forms around it — tabs, address bar, and window controls appearing one by one. The browser floats at a 15° tilt in aurora space. In the top-right corner, a glowing Publish button pulses. A 3D cursor clicks it; the button depresses and rebounds, sending an energy wave across the browser. A green lock icon lights up in the address bar, while surrounding floating geometries flash green in sequence. A soft aurora halo surrounds the browser.\n\n(0:11–0:15)\nThe browser window and all floating geometries rapidly collapse toward the center. Glass panels shatter into particles and all elements compress into a bright violet-blue core, which pulses once. The core then disperses into large white text: From idea to live, in one conversation. The words expand outward from the center with a soft elastic bounce, hold briefly on a clean aurora gradient background, then fade apart. From the same center point, the [Brand Name] logo fades in smoothly.\n\n2. Based on the knowledge you have acquired, create:\nA multi-shot storyboard script\nPrompt text approaching the 1,000-character limit\nA SeeDance video script matching the user’s current brand\n3. Activate All-Round Mode in SeeDance.Injection\npreset reference video (no need to scan the materials I gave you, just upload them directly), captured reference images (webpage screenshots without human faces, such as hook interfaces, usage scenario interfaces, core value interfaces and influence data interfaces, no more than 12 images) and the brand logo into SeeDance.",
